Build the host signing tools against OpenSSL 4, which removed the ENGINE API.

Compile the PKCS#11 ENGINE code in lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c only when OpenSSL
still provides engines (before 4.0, without OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE or
OPENSSL_NO_DEPRECATED_3_0). Without it, mkimage -N fails with an error
instead of signing with a key file, and lib/aes/aes-encrypt.c drops its
unused engine.h include. Signing with key files is unchanged, and on
OpenSSL 3 the ENGINE path is built as before.

This is not U-Boot PR #918 (a81cb0932dce, "Add support for OpenSSL
Provider API"). That patch also adds a pkcs11 provider path, but it
ignores -N on OpenSSL 3 and can sign with the wrong key from a multi-key
file, so it is not carried here.

